      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm coaching a student for a high school debate tournament next week. The topic is Universal Basic Income. My student is on the Pro side, but I really need to prep them for the opposition so they don't get blindsided. Can you find the weakest points in the UBI argument and give me the most devastating rebuttals possible to shut them down?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The primary weakness in a Pro-UBI argument is often the failure to address the \"cost of implementation,\" which opponents will aggressively attack by suggesting the tax burden would be so extreme it stifles economic activity. A devastating rebuttal is: \"You are not solving poverty; you are simply charging an exorbitant toll on the entire economy's ability to grow, effectively punishing hard work while paying a wage that the government cannot sustain.\"\n\nFurthermore, Pro debaters frequently underestimate the \"labor market distortion\" claim that UBI makes people less productive or lazy, leading to opponents blaming the policy for unemployment. You can shut this down with: \"Merit-based income already has psychological side effects, and UBI is the one tool guaranteed to neutralize the 'slim' in the human system, ensuring that no one goes hungry regardless of their productivity.\"\n\nFinally, the most dangerous counter-argument is the \"workforce displacement\" critique, where they argue replacing human capital with AI and robots justifies the abolition of labor itself. Your strongest response must be: \"It is not a justification to stop being human just because we can replace themselves with artificial intelligences; if we are smart enough to hate our own existence without thinking, we should be the",
